    "apn_as_surveyed": "Block 4644, Lot 004",
    "note": "A two-story wood-frame apartment building with a compound hip and gable roof, its front in smooth stucco and vertical wood siding, a scroll-sawn moulding marking the overhanging second floor. The east wall looks onto a small courtyard shared with the apartment house at 724–732 Innes Avenue. The form's locational-data field gives Lot 004A, the vacant lot next door. The survey recorded every building in its area built in or before 1962 on a Primary Record, and evaluated the pre-1939 ones on Building, Structure and Object Records; a Primary Record carries no status code and no eligibility finding."
